# SFX layer: shared spectral trim experiment (14 October 2026)

## 1. What the SFX reference signal is, and how the official event score is made (14 October 2026)

1. There is no clean "SFX stem". The reference of an event is the Demucs htdemucs stem(s) it was DETECTED on (drums, bass, other; a swell is "drums+bass+other"), decoded mono at 48 kHz, so it still carries the music bleed of that stem (analysis only, never written out).
2. The window of an event is [windowStart, windowEnd] from `zrmd/audio/segment.py`: preRoll before the detection to the point where the bed (drums+bass+other) has fallen endDb below its peak, capped by transientMaxSeconds / windowMaxSeconds and by the NEXT event on the same stem. Measured on Opus and OneKey: 0.18 to 1.81 s, mostly 0.49 to 0.54 s.
3. Our side is one bank chain per event (`zrmd/audio/bank.py`, fitted by `dfit`), rendered mono and placed at windowStart; per stem a track `sfx_by_stem` is the sum of the bodies of that stem's events (this is what `verify.report` reads for timing).
4. The official event score is `fit.score_window(ours, window)["ploss"]`: `ploss.score` with the seed-invariant variant OFF, `100 * 0.99 ** E2`, E2 = stft (multi-resolution 256 / 1024 / 4096 cell-wise log magnitude, JND 2 dB) + mel (64 bands, JND 2 dB) + envelope (10 ms, JND 1 dB) + onset (ms / 10), all weighted by (max(ref, ours) - floor), floor 60 dB under the loudest reference cell.
5. The SFX score of a member is the loudness-weighted mean (10^(levelDb/20)) of the event scores (`verify.report`, "sfx"); B1 (`describe.compare`, summary descriptors) is an audit, never optimised.
6. The official metric compares CELLS, so a noise is asked to reproduce the exact noise realisation of the reference: a chain rendered with another seed scores 86 to 91 against itself (identity ceiling, `sfxtrim.identity_ceiling`), 100 only for a deterministic chain. The seed-invariant variant (expected spectrum, 1.5 dB dead zone) is the metric that can reach 99.9 for noise.
7. The music critic is another metric: third-octave band power, 4096 FFT, 46 ms frames, JND 2 dB (`params/music-trim.json` specs.critic). It is smooth in frequency, so a gain can reach 99.9 on it; the official SFX loss is cell-exact.

## 2. The decisive experiment, claude-opus-5-5 (V_009 chains, 8 events, loudness-weighted means, 14 October 2026)

Script `Scripts/SfxSpectral.py experiment --slug claude-opus-5-5`, numbers in `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/logs/sfx-spectral/claude-opus-5-5.json`. official = cell-exact event score (ploss), sto = the same loss with its seed-invariant variant, critic = the music's third-octave critic, audit = mean of the held-out layouts (never optimised). Identity ceiling of the member (weighted): 96.89.

| stage | official | sto | B1 | critic | audit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| raw chain | 78.79 | 93.45 | 39.9 | 92.67 | 92.62 |
| per-event EQ (existing) | 91.38 | 99.22 | 64.0 | 97.98 | 97.75 |
| shared trim "fine" alone | 94.98 | 99.71 | 94.7 | 99.89 | 99.72 |
| shared trim "full" (music layouts) | 95.24 | 99.86 | 97.7 | 99.96 | 99.62 |
| fine then EQ (the pipeline) | 96.89 | 99.97 | 97.0 | 99.84 | 99.78 |
| full then EQ | 96.78 | 99.97 | 97.4 | 99.85 | 99.72 |
| EQ then fine | 95.93 | 99.87 | 86.9 | 99.93 | 99.83 |
| whole SFX track per stem, fine (variant a) | 95.14 | 99.64 | 96.6 | 99.82 | 99.69 |

Variants tried and dropped: no fill carriers and no finisher ("fine-plain") 92.83; third-octave critic only 78.02 (a spec that is also the score proves nothing on another one); a closed-form broadband envelope stage between the two (E001 93.62 against 94.13, E001 with EQ 96.76 against 97.95); the shared trim written back as a 120-band 2048/256 gain table (E001 94.1 to 85.8, E002 95.5 to 87.6, E003 95.7 to 87.5: no single gain table holds it, so the cooked body is stored baked); eq 150 steps instead of 500 (E001 96.26 against 97.95, E003 95.98 against 97.11).

Guards of the music that must be OFF for a short effect (measured on E001, E003, E005, E008, shared trim alone, official): minResolvedBins 2 and 18 Hz high-pass both on 91.0 / 88.5 / 93.7 / 91.1; both off 94.1 / 95.7 / 95.9 / 94.4. The high-pass doubles the envelope error of a 0.5 s window.

## 3. What "99.9 for SFX" means, and the corpus (14 October 2026, pipeline = shared trim `full` then EQ, baked)

Gate (`params/sfx-trim.json`, `gate`): HEADLINE = official loss with its seed-invariant variant >= 99.9 AND mean of the held-out audit layouts >= 99.0; MUSIC = third-octave critic >= 99.9 (reported beside); exact official score and identity ceiling reported, never a gate.

